// Refuse every delete, whatever a permit says.
//
// A forbid survives a widening; a permit does not. A later `permit fs:delete` cannot
// beat this rule, so a broad filesystem policy can still carve out deletes. There are
// no action groups, so this refuses `fs:delete` only, not `fs:move` or `fs:write`.

@id("no_deletes")
@description("This workload cannot delete files. Overwrite in place, move to a trash directory, or ask the operator to add a delete rule.")
forbid (principal, action == Box::Action::"fs:delete", resource);
